# Line-ending policy is part of this project's reproducibility contract. Recorded
# SHA256 fingerprints must resolve to the same bytes on every platform and every
# clone, regardless of the contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Repository canonical form for text files is LF (blob and index). Two classes of
# file need different worktree handling:
#
#   * Source files (run.py, src/**, requirements/**) are text. `text=auto` keeps
#     them LF in the repository. Their recorded worktree hashes were produced on
#     the Windows build host with CRLF, so they remain checkout-dependent; the
#     v2 record re-hashes source for information only and never asserts it.
#   * data/raw/** and the checked-in result CSVs are byte-fingerprinted
#     (run.json forecast_sha256, rolling_backtest.json history_sha256,
#     tools/audit_results.py, tools/audit_loss_versions.py). `text eol=crlf`
#     forces the CRLF worktree bytes the records were produced from on *every*
#     platform, including Linux CI and macOS, so those assertions hold off
#     Windows too.
#
# The blob for both classes stays LF, so no historical commit is rewritten.

* text=auto

# Binary artifacts are never line-ending converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xls  binary
*.pdf  binary

# Byte-fingerprinted tabular inputs: worktree must stay CRLF everywhere.
# `**` (unlike `*`) crosses directories, so nested output_result/ CSVs match.
data/raw/**                 text eol=crlf
results/question1/**/*.csv  text eol=crlf
results/question2/**/*.csv  text eol=crlf
results/question3/**/*.csv  text eol=crlf
results/question4/**/*.csv  text eol=crlf

# Experiment evidence is preserved byte-for-byte across Git checkouts.
# Line-ending conversion would invalidate recorded SHA256 fingerprints.
results/experiments/** -text whitespace=blank-at-eol,blank-at-eof,space-before-tab,cr-at-eol
